From 2420da661b12bd461c77a81f29a7270e47bff309 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:57:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] EVOLUTION_PATHS: 16-bit Digimon ids
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Step 3 of docs/mods/ids.md (§ 10). EVOLUTION_PATHS.from/to were s8, so a
Digimon above 127 could not be an evolution source or target. They are
DigimonId (int16_t) now; the evolution target walkers and
calculateRequirementScore carry the id as DigimonId. The table is 682
bytes larger and lives only in the executable.

The initializer wrote "none" as 0xff, which only meant -1 in an s8; it
is -1 now, and the one 0xfe entry (-2 as s8, read as such by the
original) is -2. The values are checked equal to the original table.

---
 include/dw/evl.h     |   4 +-
 src/main/evolution.c | 244 +++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 2 files changed, 124 insertions(+), 124 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/dw/evl.h b/include/dw/evl.h
index e557da8..5ccc8f4 100644
--- a/include/dw/evl.h
+++ b/include/dw/evl.h
@@ -39,8 +39,8 @@ typedef struct {
 } EvoStatsGains;
 
 typedef struct {
-	int8_t from[5];
-	int8_t to[6];
+	DigimonId from[5]; /* MOD: was s8 (ids.md step 3); -1 = none */
+	DigimonId to[6];
 } EvolutionPath;
 
 typedef struct {
